# A toolpath is a DELIVERABLE, not source. core.autocrlf=true was rewriting every .gcode on
# checkout, so a clean clone produced a file whose bytes — and therefore whose SHA-256 in the
# specimen manifests — differed from the one measured and shipped. It is not academic: the harvested
# Bambu start blocks are CRLF exports, and the header-rewrite bug of 2026-10-02 (anchored patterns
# ending on `$` not matching a line that ends `\r`) was exactly a line-ending bug in this file class.
# These travel byte for byte.
*.gcode -text
*.3mf   -text
*.stl   -text
*.png   -text
*.gguf  -text
